<!-- STEP 5: Exam Simulation -->
<section id="step5">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="sec-tag">STEP 05 · EXAM SIMULATION (4 PROBLEMS)</span>
    <h2 class="sec-title">고등부 수능/내신 실전 변형 문제</h2>

    <!-- 문제 1: 문맥상 부적절한 어휘 파악 -->
    <div class="exam-item">
      <h4>[변형 1] 다음 글의 밑줄 친 부분 중, 문맥상 낱말의 쓰임이 적절하지 않은 것은? (어휘 파악)</h4>
      <div class="exam-passage">
        Progressive educators are developing curricula to teach attention literacy. This means helping students recognize how the architecture of social media is <b>① deliberately</b> designed to distract them. Now classes include understanding the role of algorithms and observing one’s own patterns of distraction. A student might track how often they switch tasks to <b>② diminish</b> self-awareness about fragmentation. Another lesson involves unpacking the design of popular apps: Why does an app use infinite scrolling? By treating these as deliberate design choices often rooted in <b>③ psychology</b> and profit motives, young people become more <b>④ critical</b> users rather than <b>⑤ passive</b> consumers.
      </div>
      <div class="exam-choices">
        ① deliberately &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ② diminish &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ③ psychology &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ④ critical &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ⑤ passive
      </div>
      <details>
        <summary>정답 및 해설 확인</summary>
        <div class="answer-content">
          <b>정답: ② (diminish → raise 또는 heighten)</b><br>
          <b>해설:</b> 학생들이 숙제하는 동안 휴대폰을 확인하거나 작업을 전환하는 횟수를 추적하는 활동은 자신의 주의력 분절(fragmentation) 상태를 자각하고 이를 줄이기 위해 '자기 인식(self-awareness)을 높이기 위한(raise)' 목적이다. 인식을 줄인다는 뜻의 diminish는 글의 흐름에 정면으로 위배된다.
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <!-- 문제 2: 빈칸 추론 -->
    <div class="exam-item">
      <h4>[변형 2] 다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것을 고르시오. (빈칸 추론)</h4>
      <div class="exam-passage">
        Traditional media literacy focused heavily on determining whether an information source could be trusted. Today, however, educators are expanding this scope toward attention literacy. By examining why applications employ endless feeds, distinctive sound cues, and engaging color palettes, students begin to realize that digital platforms are not neutral tools. Instead, they discover that digital interfaces are engineered purposefully to capture human attention for financial gain. As students learn to perceive these features as calculated corporate strategies, they can transform themselves from ____________________________________.
      </div>
      <div class="exam-choices">
        ① uncritical technology skeptics into avid online app developers<br>
        ② passive consumers into more critical, conscious digital users<br>
        ③ solitary internet learners into highly cooperative social members<br>
        ④ distracted multitasking individuals into completely isolated users<br>
        ⑤ commercial product buyers into aggressive media creators
      </div>
      <details>
        <summary>정답 및 해설 확인</summary>
        <div class="answer-content">
          <b>정답: ②</b><br>
          <b>해설:</b> 지문의 핵심 결론인 'young people become more critical users rather than passive consumers'를 그대로 반영한 선택지이다. 플랫폼의 이면에 깔린 심리학적 기제와 수익 동기를 이해함으로써 무비판적으로 이끌려 다니던 수동적 소비자(passive consumers)에서 비판적이고 주체적인 사용자(critical, conscious digital users)로 거듭난다는 내용이 적절하다.
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <!-- 문제 3: 문장 삽입 -->
    <div class="exam-item">
      <h4>[변형 3] 글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳을 고르시오. (문장 삽입)</h4>
      <div class="exam-passage">
        <b>[주어진 문장]</b><br>
        A student might be tasked with tracking how many times they switch tasks or check their phone in an hour of homework, to raise self-awareness about fragmentation.<br><br>
        Classes in media literacy traditionally cover how to evaluate the credibility of sources ― now they also include recognizing clickbait, understanding the role of algorithms in what content is served up, and observing one’s own patterns of distraction. ( ① ) Another lesson might involve unpacking the design of popular apps. ( ② ) Why does an app use infinite scrolling instead of pages? ( ③ ) Why do notifications appear with specific colors and sounds? ( ④ ) By treating these as deliberate design choices (often rooted in psychology and profit motives), young people become more critical users rather than passive consumers. ( ⑤ )
      </div>
      <div class="exam-choices">
        ① &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ② &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ③ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ④ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ⑤
      </div>
      <details>
        <summary>정답 및 해설 확인</summary>
        <div class="answer-content">
          <b>정답: ①</b><br>
          <b>해설:</b> 앞선 문장의 끝부분에서 제시된 '자신의 산만함 패턴을 관찰하는 것(observing one’s own patterns of distraction)'에 대한 구체적 실천 과제가 바로 주어진 문장의 '학생이 숙제 중 작업 전환이나 휴대폰 확인 횟수를 추적하는 활동'이다. 또한 주어진 문장 바로 뒤의 문장이 'Another lesson(또 다른 수업)'으로 자연스럽게 추가 사례(앱 디자인 해체)를 도입하고 있으므로 주어진 문장의 위치는 ①이 가장 타당하다.
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <!-- 문제 4: 서술형 조건영작 -->
    <div class="exam-item">
      <h4>[변형 4] 다음 우리말 해석에 맞도록 &lt;조건&gt;에 제시된 단어들을 바르게 배열하여 문장을 완성하시오. (서술형)</h4>
      <div class="exam-passage">
        <b>[우리말 해석]</b><br>
        "이것들을 의도적인 디자인 선택으로 대함으로써, 젊은이들은 수동적인 소비자라기보다는 더 비판적인 사용자가 된다."<br><br>
        <b>&lt;조건&gt;</b><br>
        1. 아래 제시된 단어 및 어구를 반드시 모두 한 번씩만 사용할 것.<br>
        [ By treating / young people / as deliberate design choices / rather than / become / these / passive consumers / more critical users ]<br>
        2. 어형 변화 없이 온전한 한 문장으로 완성할 것.
      </div>
      <details>
        <summary>정답 및 해설 확인</summary>
        <div class="answer-content">
          <b>[모범 답안]</b><br>
          <b>By treating these as deliberate design choices, young people become more critical users rather than passive consumers.</b><br><br>
          <b>[채점 기준 및 해설]</b><br>
          - 전치사구 부사절: By treating(동명사) + 목적어(these) + 목적격보어(as deliberate design choices) 구조를 바르게 형성했는가?<br>
          - 주절: 주어(young people) + 동사(become) + 보어(more critical users) + 대비 연결어구(rather than passive consumers) 어순을 오차 없이 배치했는가?
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

